Other parts of this project are MIT, and are not covered by this document:
the SDK and its public headers, the plugin examples, the Permission plugin, and
Conan Shop. Each carries its own LICENSE file.


WHAT YOU MAY DO

  Write plugins that use this API, and do whatever you like with them,
  including SELLING them. The plugin is yours; its licence is your choice, and
  you need no permission, owe no fee, and share nothing.

  Run this API on as many servers as you like, including servers that charge
  their players.

  Download this API through the official channel: this repository's Releases
  page.

  Share and index the LINK to this repository anywhere: a website, a forum, a
  video, a marketplace, a resource list. The link is free.

  Copy, modify and redistribute the EXAMPLES from the SDK as the basis for your
  own plugins.

  Study the headers.


WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

  Use this API commercially. It may not be sold, licensed, rented, offered as
  part of a paid service, or included in any commercial package.

  Re-host the files. Do not mirror the download on another site, do not
  redistribute the .tar.gz, and do not include the binaries or headers in
  another package, modpack or installer. Whoever wants the API gets it from the
  official repository: share the link, not the file.

  Use this material to create another plugin API for Conan Exiles, derived or
  otherwise.

  Redistribute this SDK as your own, or as part of another SDK.


WHY THE SPLIT

  The API is the foundation: it is where the mechanics of how things work
  internally live, and it stays with whoever maintains it. This exists so that
  there is ONE foundation, with an upgrade path when the game changes, rather
  than five diverging copies nobody can keep track of.

  What you build on top is a different matter, and it is yours. Selling a plugin
  is legitimate and expected; nothing here gets in the way of that.


NO WARRANTY

  This software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. It runs
  inside a game server's process and may crash it. The authors are not liable
  for data loss, downtime, or any damage arising from its use.


